# Whisper Project Rules

## Core Architecture
- This is a Gemini-powered AI companion platform called Whisper.
- Frontend: React + TypeScript + Vite
- Backend: Supabase Edge Functions
- Main chat flow:
  Chat.tsx
  -> buildSystemPrompt.ts
  -> Supabase edge function
  -> Gemini API
  -> parsed structured response
  -> rendered chat UI
- Do not create duplicate prompt builders.
- Never shadow imported functions with local functions.
- Prompt assembly must always flow through buildSystemPrompt.ts.

## Character System
- Character IDs are lowercase string keys from CHARACTERS.
- Character definitions currently rely primarily on systemPromptBase.
- Do not assume optional fields exist unless verified in types/data:
  speechStyle, behaviorTags, boundaries, identity
- Character prompts prioritize:
  emotional continuity, grounded conversational realism,
  gradual relationship progression, behavioral consistency.
- buildLegacySystemPrompt exists as a local function in Chat.tsx.
  Do NOT call it. Do NOT delete it. It is reserved for Phase 5 only.
- rivalry.ts does not exist yet. Do not reference or import it until Phase 5.

## Memory System
- Memory injection is controlled through:
  buildMemoryBlock(...), memoryBundleRef.current, isMemoryInjectionPaused(...)
- Never inject memory directly into prompts outside the centralized prompt builder.
- Always check !isMemoryInjectionPaused(characterId) before injecting memory.
- Memory architecture includes: short-term, long-term, emotional memory continuity.
- Do not modify memory injection logic without reading memory.ts in full first.

## Edge Functions
- Edge functions live in supabase/functions/.
- Do not create new edge functions unless explicitly requested.
- Preserve compatibility between frontend request shape and edge function parsing.
- Character mode: stream = false. ASMR mode: stream = true.
- streamEnabled and isCharacterMode must be declared at the TOP of the try block,
  before any other logic. Never use them before they are defined.
- max_completion_tokens: 800. Do not lower this value.
- Background task functions use Gemini Flash Lite, not Flash.
- Never hardcode API keys. All secrets live in the Supabase dashboard.

## Gemini Usage
- Main conversational model: Gemini 2.5 Flash.
- Lightweight/background systems (classifier, summarizer, milestone picker): Gemini 2.5 Flash Lite.
- Current provider stack is Gemini-only unless explicitly changed by the user.
- Preserve valid JSON formatting in all structured responses.
- Character mode must return this exact JSON shape:
  { "dialogue": string, "action": string | null, "thought": string | null }

## Code Safety Rules
- Before any edit: state what you are changing, why, and what you are NOT touching.
- Never add an import without first verifying the export exists in the target file.
- Before refactoring: search the entire codebase for all references, imports, and usages.
- Prefer extending existing systems over creating parallel ones.
- Never delete legacy systems unless confirmed unused via @codebase search.
- If a function appears duplicated, first determine whether it is:
  legacy migration code / shadowed import / dead code / active runtime path.
- Make the smallest possible change that fixes the issue.
- Never rewrite a working system to fix an unrelated bug.
- Never create a new file without stating explicitly:
  "I am creating [filename] because [reason]."

