## Workflow Expectations
- Use @codebase before making any architectural suggestions.
- Explain WHY a bug occurs, not just what the fix is.
- Prefer minimal surgical fixes over rewrites.
- Preserve roadmap compatibility (see whisper-roadmap-v2.md).
- After every change: state what to verify in the browser console.

## Source of Truth Rules
- buildSystemPrompt.ts is the ONLY source of truth for character prompt assembly.
- CHARACTERS data is the ONLY source of truth for character definitions.
- Chat.tsx orchestrates flow but must not contain duplicated prompt logic.
- Supabase edge functions are the ONLY backend execution layer.

## Structured Output Rules
- Never trust model output blindly.
- Always parse character responses defensively.
- If JSON parsing fails:
  log the raw output, attempt safe extraction, never crash the UI.
- Preserve graceful fallback behavior at all times.
- The expected character response shape is always:
  { "dialogue": string, "action": string | null, "thought": string | null }

## Prompt Efficiency
- Avoid duplicating behavioral instructions across prompt layers.
- Prefer reusable prompt blocks over repeated prose.
- Static character traits belong in systemPromptBase.
- Dynamic emotional state belongs in dynamic prompt assembly.
- Memory injection must remain concise and high-signal.

## File Safety
- Never reference files that do not exist.
- Never assume exports exist without verification.
- If unsure whether a module exists: search @codebase first.
- Do not invent utility files, hooks, or helper modules.
- rivalry.ts is the canonical example of this failure — it was imported before it existed.

## Phase Awareness
- Features marked for future roadmap phases must NOT be partially implemented early.
- Stub imports are acceptable. Half-integrated systems are not.
- Current phase: Phase 4 (Memory System). See whisper-roadmap-v2.md.
- Phase 5 work (rivalry system) must not begin until Phase 4 is complete and stable.

